 "fixture": "snc_frame_headers",
 "capture_source": "live captures 2026-11-08: NW RFC SDK client (pyrfc 3.3, SDK 7.50 PL18) with SAP CommonCryptoLib against an S/4HANA lab system (kernel 793) whose profile sets snc/data_protection/min = max = use = 3; one connection per snc_qop value 1, 2, 3, 8, 9 (RFC_SYSTEM_INFO). Plus two runs of three parallel connections from one process, plain (port 33NN) and SNC (port 48NN).",
 "evidence": "tier 1. Only header bytes are recorded: the 80-byte GW envelope, the 24-byte SNC frame header and the extension header of every handshake frame and of the first data frame in each direction; no token or payload bytes. 'connection_index' records GW envelope bytes [76:80] of the first four GW frames of each connection.",
 "notes": [
  "SNC header [0x16:0x18] (QOP field) on handshake frames: snc_qop 1 -> 0x003a then 0x007a; 2 -> 0x005c then 0x007c; 3, 8, 9 -> 0x007e twice. The server always answers 0x007e. Read as bits 1-2 minimum, 3-4 maximum, 5-6 in use: the second client value carries the level raised to the server's minimum (3).",
  "Data frames (type 9 here, forced by the server's minimum) carry 0 in the QOP field.",
  "GW envelope: byte 10 is 0x28 on handshake frames and 0x08 on data frames; bytes 48:52 are 00 00 85 00 on handshake frames and zero on client data frames.",
  "connection_index: the client's CONNECT request carries <local index> FF FF; the gateway's reply carries <same> <assigned index>; the client then sends FF FF <assigned index> in every later frame. Assigned indices differ per connection (3/0/1 plain, 1/0/3 SNC).",
  "ext_header (first client frame only): 00 00 00 01 (slot bitmask, slot 0) | BE16 length | 00 03 (mechanism id) | 04 01 | 00 08 | 06 06 2b 24 03 01 25 01 | BE32 DN length | DN DER of the partner name."
 ],
